WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.304
We are following the

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.839
latest developments from Ukraine,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:06.840
where the military says

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.141
Russian forces are keeping up

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.876
a high rate of rocket attacks.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.678
On the front lines in the east.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.612
Ukraine says nearly

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.347
two dozen attacks were carried out

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.548
in just a 24 hour

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.516
period, primarily

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.851
focused in several cities

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.786
in Donetsk, including back Mount

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.921
and then the Turkish region as well.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.722
Ukraine's military

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.158
also says Russia has set records.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.659
They say hitting Ukraine's

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.428
east with artillery fire,

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.630
including in the Luhansk region.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.297
Now, over the weekend,

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.932
Ukraine reported a massive barrage

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.134
of Russian attacks

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.435
right across the country.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.003
Russia says it targeted key

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.171
energy facilities.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.507
Despite that, the Ukrainian capital

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:41.541
and several regions

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.710
were able to avoid power cuts on Sunday.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.445
President Vladimir Zelinski credits

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.080
those working to restore power.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:48.982
Mr.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.216
Putin, there is

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:50.617
the very

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.451
fact that after

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.886
constant terrorist attacks

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.854
with rockets and showerhead drones,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.923
after a massive missile strike this week,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.591
we can have such peaceful energy

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.827
days proves the professionalism

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.062
of our energy workers

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.097
and the extraordinary dedication

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:04.831
of everyone

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.900
who works to preserve our energy system.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.001
My animals,

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.002
we have to realize

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.037
this is not yet a decisive victory

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.338
on the energy front.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.373
Unfortunately,

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.541
there may be new terrorist

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.443
attacks from Russia.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.144
CNN's David McKenzie

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.579
is following the latest developments

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.449
for us from Kiev.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.284
In the last several days here in Ukraine,

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.086
the heaviest fighting has happened

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.188
on the eastern front of this conflict.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.323
Ukrainian and Russian sources

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.658
even saying that

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.660
the Russian mechanized brigade

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.562
trying to push through the town.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.431
Volodya saw significant losses.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.365
And you see this

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.935
dramatic video of them being pushed back.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.070
Sustained casualties

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.239
from drone and artillery strikes.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.841
Now, the Defense Intelligence

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.842
of the United Kingdom

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.510
saying this is the worst period

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.745
of casualties for the Russians

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.981
since the very start of this war.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.316
That's hard to stack up,

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.717
but certainly it's been

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.986
a very intense period of fighting there.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.056
The Russian forces have had the forces

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.390
and in fact,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.959
private military contractors

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.693
have had

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.760
somewhat more success

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.729
to the north of that town

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:10.864
in the Barmouth area.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:14.267
But you're not seeing significant gains

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.068
of territory

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.370
in this period of attritional warfare.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.173
Here in this conflict in Kiev

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.408
and the surrounds of the capital.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.576
They are saying they have managed

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.012
to keep the lights on throughout the day,

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.214
which is a significant achievement,

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.883
says the energy minister,

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.385
because of those recent attacks

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.754
by missiles and drones by the Russians,

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.022
that many of them,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.757
which the Ukrainians manage

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.092
to shoot down.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.161
He also saying the repair work

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.496
is enabling them to keep the lights on.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.564
That's significant

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.798
because Russia was looking

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.367
to break the spirit

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.736
of Ukrainian civilians

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.504
by targeting infrastructure,

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.772
something they haven't

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.107
been able to achieve.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.209
David McKenzie, CNN, Kiev.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:56.943
CNN Scott

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.244
McLean, is following developments

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.312
and joins us in London

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.747
now with the latest.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.248
Scott, the head of the

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.816
a mercenary group goes

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.952
and has been talking about how essential

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.153
it is for the Russians

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.221
to capture back market

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.055
if they want to have,

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.757
I think you said, an easier time

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.759
basically capturing the rest of the east.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.360
What are we hearing about the progress

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:14.928
there making?

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:15.828
It's pretty remarkable

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.330
considering the fact is a town

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.766
that surely very few people outside of

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.000
Ukraine would have even heard of

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:21.701
before the war.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.235
Now it has

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.803
this really outsized importance

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.438
and it's that way for a few reasons.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.906
A, it's been really a brick wall

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.907
for the Russians

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.142
for months and months

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.310
who've been trying to capture it.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:30.977
And part of the reason

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:31.678
that they've had such

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.479
difficulty is because it is extremely

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.814
well fortified, both

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.683
naturally and militarily.

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.951
And so the Russians have

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:39.686
exhausted a

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:40.620
huge number of people,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.721
a huge number of equipment,

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.722
and actually trying to take it

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.723
with really no luck.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.425
And so as of late, their strategy

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.760
instead has been to go around it

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.229
to try to surround it.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.730
And there are some indications

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.732
that they're having making progress.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:53.900
Ukrainian military said

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.268
that there have been fierce battles

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:56.069
in towns

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.503
to the north of back

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.238
mud and also

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.773
to the west of Back Mount as well.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.508
Which is concerning.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.776
The Ukrainians also acknowledge

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:04.110
that, look,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.247
their access in and out has been sporadic

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.481
as of late has been difficult

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.782
because many of the main routes

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:10.550
have been cut off.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.551
And now just this morning,

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:12.018
we're learning

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.386
that the Bognor private

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.587
military contractor

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.623
claims to have captured

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.258
this town called Crossing of Horror,

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:20.493
which is just north of Park Moot.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:20.893
In fact,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.263
they posted a picture with their fighters

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.230
standing at the

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.798
southwest corner of the town.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:26.699
And so

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.101
all of this paints a picture

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.902
that's not good for the Ukrainians,

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.237
despite the fact that Ukraine says

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.872
that, look, it's not

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:33.573
the Russians

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.407
that are wearing down

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.441
the Ukrainian troops

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.542
in the Ukrainian resolve.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.510
They say that it's actually

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.111
the opposite,

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:38.978
that the

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.380
Ukrainians are rushing down

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.481
the Russians ability

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.016
to launch a major attack.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.183
But this is pretty

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.885
optimistic view of a situation

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.654
that clearly is very difficult

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:48.655
for the Ukrainians.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.022
And, of course,

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.790
we've seen this movie before

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.892
with several towns in that area where,

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.126
you know,

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.594
the Russians don't make any huge

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.295
one fell swoop

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.229
kind of breakthroughs,

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.431
but it's just sort of this slow

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.799
grinding move forward.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:00.967
And that seems to be

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.735
what we're seeing now there today.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:03.870
Scott McClain, thank you.

